{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And he said: For a hand is upon the throne of YH, etc. — therefore I call the name of the altar 'YHWH is my banner.' Like a person's name, Eliezer or Ammanu-El, for the Holy One, blessed be He, raised His hand upon His throne and swore that there is war against Amalek from generation to generation — like ״כי אשא אל שמים ידי״. This is the principal plain sense. And some interpret: when my hand and strength are upon the throne of YH, which is the throne of the King of Israel, then there will be war against Amalek. And it does not seem right to me at all, for it would have to say כי תהיה יד — but the yod above applies, as I explained, and its meaning is: for a hand is upon the throne of YH."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Rashbam reads the י of כי as possessive ('my hand') but argues the syntax points instead to כִּי meaning 'for/that', with the phrase הרים הקב\"ה את ידו as the implied subject."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:55.222950425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}